# Datasets

This project uses two publicly available 2D biomedical image segmentation datasets.
The datasets are NOT included in this repository due to size and licensing restrictions.
Please download them from the official sources below.

---

## 1. DRIVE – Digital Retinal Images for Vessel Extraction

- Task: Retinal vessel segmentation
- Total Images: 40 fundus photographs (20 train / 20 test)
- Resolution: 565 × 584 pixels
- Challenge: Thin and branching vessel structures

Download:
- Official: https://drive.grand-challenge.org/
- Kaggle:   https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/andrewmvd/drive-digital-retinal-images-for-vessel-extraction

Preprocessing applied:
- CLAHE enhancement for vessel contrast
- Normalization
- Resized to 256x256

---

## 2. ISIC-2017 – Skin Lesion Segmentation Challenge

- Task: Dermoscopic skin lesion segmentation
- Total Images: 2000 training / 150 validation / 600 test
- Challenge: Irregular shapes and unclear lesion boundaries

Download:
- Official: https://challenge.isic-archive.com/data/#2017
- Kaggle:   https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/humansintheloop/skin-lesions-isic-2017

Preprocessing applied:
- Normalization to reduce illumination variations
- Resized to 256x256

---

After downloading, place the datasets inside this Datasets/ folder before running any notebooks.
